.TH RAIN 1 "April 2026" "rain 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rain \- terminal ASCII rain animation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rain
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-init\-config
.RB [ \-\-force ]]
.RB [ \-\-help | \-h ]
.RB [ \-\-version | \-V ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rain
draws an ASCII rain animation in the terminal using ncurses.
The animation runs continuously until the configured quit key is
pressed and survives terminal resize without flicker.
.PP
With no options the program loads its configuration from the first
available source (see
.BR CONFIGURATION )
and starts the animation. If no configuration file is found,
built-in defaults are used.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " path"
Load configuration from
.IR path
instead of searching the default locations. A missing or
unreadable file is silently ignored and built-in defaults are used.
.TP
.B \-\-init\-config
Write a starter configuration file to the default location, or to
.I path
if combined with
.BR \-\-config .
By default refuses to overwrite an existing file.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Allow
.B \-\-init\-config
to overwrite an existing file. Has no effect on its own.
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Print a short help message on standard output and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-V
Print the program version on standard output and exit.
.SH KEYS
While the animation is running:
.TP
.B q
Quit. Configurable through the
.B quit_key
option (see
.BR CONFIGURATION ).
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B rain
loads configuration from the first available source, in this order:
.IP 1. 4
The path passed to
.BR \-\-config .
.IP 2. 4
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/rain/config .
.IP 3. 4
.IR $HOME/.config/rain/config .
.PP
The configuration format is one
.IR key " = " value
pair per line. Lines starting with
.B #
and blank lines are ignored. Unknown keys and malformed lines emit
a warning on standard error and are otherwise skipped.
.PP
All keys are optional. Run
.B rain \-\-init\-config
to drop an annotated starter file at the default location.
.SS Available keys
.TP
.B frame_delay_ms
Delay between frames, in milliseconds. Lower values produce a
faster fall. Must be positive. Default:
.BR 40 .
.TP
.B density
Drop density, expressed as drops per terminal column. Must be
positive. Default:
.BR 0.5 .
.TP
.B speed_min
Minimum drop speed in rows per frame. Must be positive. Default:
.BR 1 .
.TP
.B speed_max
Maximum drop speed in rows per frame. Must be positive. Default:
.BR 5 .
If
.B speed_min
exceeds
.B speed_max
the values are swapped and a warning is printed.
.TP
.B quit_key
Single-character key that terminates the animation. Default:
.BR q .
.TP
.B color_mode
Selects the palette source. Either
.B auto
(generate a gradient by darkening
.BR color_base )
or
.B manual
(use the explicit
.B colors
list). Default:
.BR manual .
.TP
.B color_base
Base color for
.BR "color_mode = auto" ,
in
.B #rrggbb
form. Default:
.BR #ffffff .
.TP
.B colors
Comma-separated list of colors in
.B #rrggbb
form, brightest first. Should contain
.B speed_max
entries; if it does not match, the program falls back to
.BR "color_mode = auto" .
Setting this key implies
.BR "color_mode = manual" .
Default: a 5-step grayscale palette.
.TP
.B use_xterm256
When
.BR true ,
quantize colors to the built-in xterm-256 palette instead of
requesting exact RGB through
.BR init_color (3X).
Useful in terminals that advertise color-changing capability but
ignore the actual RGB values, such as some konsole, SSH and tmux
setups. Default:
.BR false .
.SH COLORS
By default
.B rain
asks the terminal to install exact RGB colors via
.BR init_color (3X).
This gives the highest palette fidelity and works in terminals
including ghostty, kitty, wezterm, xterm and alacritty.
.PP
Some terminals report support for changing colors but ignore the
actual RGB values written. The typical symptom is drops appearing
in unexpected ANSI colors, often blue-ish, instead of the configured
palette. Setting
.B use_xterm256 = true
maps colors onto the fixed xterm-256 cube and grayscale ramp,
avoiding palette mutation at the cost of slightly lower fidelity
for dim or low-chroma colors.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful run or
.B \-\-init\-config
wrote the starter configuration.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid command-line argument,
.B \-\-init\-config
refused to overwrite an existing file (without
.BR \-\-force ),
or the terminal lacks the capabilities required by the program
(no color support, cannot hide the cursor).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/rain/config
Primary default configuration path, used when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is set.
.TP
.I $HOME/.config/rain/config
Fallback default configuration path.
.TP
.I PREFIX/share/doc/rain/rain.conf.example
Annotated example configuration installed by
.BR "make install" .
.SH EXAMPLES
Run with built-in defaults:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
rain
.EE
.RE
.PP
Write a starter configuration to the default location:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
rain \-\-init\-config
.EE
.RE
.PP
Replace an existing configuration file:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
rain \-\-init\-config \-\-force
.EE
.RE
.PP
Run with a configuration file from an explicit path:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
rain \-\-config ./my-rain.conf
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ncurses (3X),
.BR init_color (3X)
.SH AUTHORS
Originally written by Nik in July 2017 and subsequently extended.
